---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Follow Along">
  <h1>Follow the demonstration</h1>
  <p>
    Watch for six visible states. Each one answers a different question about whether an
    AI-generated change is ready to ship.
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Issue —</strong> Is the intended outcome clear and testable?</li>
    <li><strong>Draft —</strong> Can we inspect exactly what the coding agent changed?</li>
    <li><strong>Review —</strong> Did an independent reviewer find code or workflow risks?</li>
    <li><strong>Fix —</strong> Were those findings converted into verified changes?</li>
    <li><strong>Gate —</strong> Will policy stop a build that still carries supply-chain risk?</li>
    <li><strong>Deploy —</strong> Did only the remediated version reach the live site?</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="card">
    <strong>The important boundary.</strong> The coding agent, reviewer, security scanners, and
    deployment policy are separate controls. No single AI decision is trusted to ship by itself.
  </div>

  <h2>Why the pipeline stops</h2>
  <p>
    The training start state deliberately uses a vulnerable Markdown dependency. The application
    builds, but the production audit rejects it. Dependabot proposes an upgrade; after that change
    passes the dependency policy, deployment can continue.
  </p>

  <h2>Explore safely</h2>
  <p>
    This repository contains deliberate training findings. Run it locally to inspect the site,
    but do not deploy the start state as a production application.
  </p>
  <pre>git clone https://github.com/anothergeorgecoldham/ship-with-ai.git
cd ship-with-ai
npm ci
npm run dev</pre>

